georust `geo` / `geo-types`                                  MIT OR Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/georust/geo
    Copyright (c) The GeoRust Developers

Portions of `crate::space::r2` — the planar `f64` geometry types (Coord, Point,
Line, LineString, Polygon, MultiPolygon, …) and the algorithms over them
(BooleanOps, Relate, Area, Centroid, Simplify, ConvexHull, Distance, Intersects,
Length, Orient, …) — are ported from `geo`/`geo-types`, mirroring their shapes
and trait names so call sites migrate by changing the import path. The
Hausdorff/Fréchet similarity measures in `crate::earth::similarity` are likewise
ported from `geo`.

================================================================================
H3 — Uber hexagonal hierarchical geospatial index            Apache-2.0
    https://github.com/uber/h3
    Copyright (c) Uber Technologies, Inc.

`crate::index::h3` (the u64 codec, the icosahedral FaceIJK gnomonic projection,
grid traversal, child enumeration, and the base-cell / face / FaceIJK constant
tables) is ported from the H3 C reference. The constant tables are lifted
verbatim. The `h3o` Rust port (https://github.com/HydroniumLabs/h3o) is used as
the porting reference and as a dev-dependency differential-test oracle; see the
h3o repository for its license.

