GeographicLib / geographiclib-rs                              MIT
    https://geographiclib.sourceforge.io
    Copyright (c) Charles F. F. Karney
    https://github.com/georust/geographiclib-rs
    Copyright (c) Federico Dolce and Michael Kirk

`crate::earth::karney` (the ellipsoidal direct/inverse geodesic solvers behind
`Ellipsoid::{inverse, direct}` and the `space::r2` `Geodesic` metric) is ported
from `geographiclib-rs`, the GeoRust port of Karney's GeographicLib. The
algorithms are from C. F. F. Karney, "Algorithms for geodesics", J. Geodesy 87,
43–55 (2013). `geographiclib-rs` is also a dev-dependency differential-test
oracle for the port.

================================================================================
Algorithm references
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The following are algorithmic provenance, not source-code ports:

  * Boolean polygon overlay — F. Martínez, A. J. Rueda, F. R. Feito,
    "A new algorithm for computing Boolean operations on polygons" (2009/2013).
    Implemented in `crate::space::r2::bool_ops`.

  * Discrete Fréchet distance — T. Eiter and H. Mannila,
    "Computing Discrete Fréchet Distance" (1994).
    Implemented in `crate::algebra::metric` / `crate::earth::similarity`.

  * Geohash — the public geohash encoding (G. M. Niemeyer).
    Reimplemented in `crate::index::geohash`.

  * `crate::space::r2::prepared` follows the design of GEOS `PreparedGeometry`.

  * `crate::simd`'s scalar-first SIMD dispatch follows the approach used by
    RustFFT.
